## aws.reach.set · hetzner apply, the role refuses the session's tags (rc 1)
🐢 heres the wave...

🔭 aws.reach.set --org acme --env test --mode apply
   ├─ profile: acme.test.ehmpath
   ├─ box:     grove (cloud@hetzner.hetzbot)
   ├─ identity: http://127.0.0.1:9911 (mirrored from [default])
   ├─ reach:   the grove's badge ⇒ arn:aws:iam::111122223333:role/grove-hop
   └─ apply
      ├─ ~/.aws/config now declares [profile acme.test.ehmpath] ✔
      ├─ gitroot: <fix>/h8d/.local/state/keyrack.gitroot (the cwd is not a repo)
      ├─ rack already answers acme.test.AWS_PROFILE = acme.test.ehmpath
      ├─ prove: aws sts get-caller-identity --profile acme.test.ehmpath
      └─ 💥 MalfunctionError: the profile is declared and does NOT answer

  aws said:
    An error occurred (AccessDenied) when calling the AssumeRole operation: User: arn:aws:sts::123456789012:assumed-role/grove-role/session is not authorized to perform: sts:TagSession on resource: arn:aws:iam::111122223333:role/grove-hop

  ⇒ the role TRUSTS this box, and refuses what its session carries (sts:TagSession)
    the principal that asked: arn:aws:sts::123456789012:assumed-role/grove-role/session
    ⇒ an IAM Roles Anywhere session carries a source identity and session tags,
      and a chained AssumeRole passes both on. the role's trust statement for
      that principal must allow all three actions — an ask of acme/infrastructure:
        "sts:AssumeRole", "sts:SetSourceIdentity", "sts:TagSession"

