🔭 aws.reach.set --org acme --env test --mode apply
   ├─ profile: acme.test.ehmpath
   ├─ box:     grove (cloud@hetzner.hetzbot)
   ├─ identity: http://127.0.0.1:9911 (mirrored from [default])
   ├─ reach:   the grove's badge ⇒ arn:aws:iam::111122223333:role/grove-hop
   └─ apply
      ├─ ~/.aws/config now declares [profile acme.test.ehmpath] ✔
      ├─ gitroot: <fix>/h8g/.local/state/keyrack.gitroot (the cwd is not a repo)
      ├─ rack does not answer acme.test.AWS_PROFILE yet
      │  vault: os.direct  (a grove)
      └─ 💥 MalfunctionError: keyrack refused the set
         ⇒ it said: keyrack: AWS_PROFILE is not declared for env=test

  why: AWS_PROFILE may not be DECLARED for env=test in this repo's
       .agent/keyrack.yml — an undeclared key stores and then reads
       'absent 🫧' forever (domain.terms/term=entry)
  fix: declare it, then re-run —
    env.test:
      - AWS_PROFILE

## aws.reach.set · hetzner apply, the set claims success and stores no value (rc 2)
🐢 heres the wave...

🔭 aws.reach.set --org acme --env test --mode apply
   ├─ profile: acme.test.ehmpath
   ├─ box:     grove (cloud@hetzner.hetzbot)
   ├─ identity: http://127.0.0.1:9911 (mirrored from [default])
   ├─ reach:   the grove's badge ⇒ arn:aws:iam::111122223333:role/grove-hop
   └─ apply
      ├─ ~/.aws/config already current for [profile acme.test.ehmpath]
      ├─ gitroot: <fix>/h8g/.local/state/keyrack.gitroot (the cwd is not a repo)
      ├─ rack does not answer acme.test.AWS_PROFILE yet
      │  vault: os.direct  (a grove)
      └─ ✋ ConstraintError: the set reported success and the rack still answers ''

  expected: acme.test.ehmpath
  ⇒ every consumer reads the rack, so each will act as ''
    no matter how correct the profile body is
  ⇒ if it still answers an EXPORTED value, the rack is shadowed:
    'os.envvar' is checked FIRST in keyrack's grant flow, so an
    AWS_PROFILE in the shell outranks every rack entry there is.
    ~/.zshenv exports one (owned by 2.5.zsh) — that is the cause.
  fix: set it by hand, and answer 'acme.test.ehmpath' at the value prompt —
    rhx keyrack set --owner ehmpath --key AWS_PROFILE \
                    --org acme --env test --vault os.direct

