        (~/.zshenv is 2.5.zsh's, and it exports no AWS_PROFILE)

## 5.6.aws verify · hetzner, the credentials file is absent (rc 1)
   • the 'ambient' profile is declared ✔
   • [profile ambient] mirrors [default]'s endpoint ✔ (http://127.0.0.1:9911)
   • [default] is infra's alone ✔ (this bundle's fence holds none)
   • the ambient profile yields live credentials ✔ (value not printed)
   • with NO profile named, a region still resolves ✔ (us-east-1)
   ✋ ConstraintError: ~/.aws/credentials is ABSENT
      ⇒ this box sets AWS_SDK_LOAD_CONFIG=1 (2.5.zsh/zshrc.sh), so aws-sdk
        v2 opens that file to derive a region and throws ENOENT when
        it is absent — even with valid credentials already in env
      fix: rhx grove.provision --what 5.6.aws --mode apply

